{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474646525,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgwMDYwNjQ5Mw=="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474647374,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0OTIzNjEzNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-249236135"},"message":"I think that could be a good point, if annex is outdated, to offer to (using ui, if ui.is_interactive) install it.\n- On Debian-based systems it could ask additionally either they might just want to enable neurodebian repo and install datalad from it (or just git-annex-standalone)\n- on other linuxes and OSX -- standalone build \n\nFTR here is the script I use to upgrade annex on OSX (wouldn't we need verification ?)\n\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n\ncurver=$(git annex version | awk '/version:/{print $3;}' | sed -e 's,-.*,,g')\nannexdir=/Applications/git-annex.app\ncurverdir=$annexdir.$curver\n\nrm -f git-annex.dmg\n# release\n# curl -O https://downloads.kitenet.net/git-annex/OSX/current/10.10_Yosemite/git-annex.dmg\n# daily build\ncurl -O https://downloads.kitenet.net/git-annex/autobuild/x86_64-apple-yosemite/git-annex.dmg\n\nhdiutil attach git-annex.dmg \n\nif [ ! -z \"$curver\" ] \u0026\u0026 [ ! -e \"$curverdir\" ]; then\n    mv $annexdir $curverdir\nfi\n\nrsync -a /Volumes/git-annex/git-annex.app /Applications/\nhdiutil  detach /Volumes/git-annex/\n```\n\nedit 1: we could probably just rely on authenticity of the connection via https to downloads.kitenet.net","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475334849,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MDkxNzQ4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-250917483"},"message":"Since get is under heavy RF, postponing since might simply be superseded","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475511057,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE0OTc4NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251149785"},"message":"Looking into this in #959:\n\nRuined my installtion for testing (git-annex v5):\n\n```\nmih@meiner /tmp/ds000001 (git)-[master] % datalad ls\n2016-10-03 18:08:53,030 [ERROR  ] stderr| git-annex: unrecognized option `--raw'\n| \n| Usage: git-annex version  [option ...]\n| \n| To see additional options common to all commands, run: git annex help options (cmd.py:406)\n/tmp/ds000001 (git)-[master] % datalad get sub-01/anat/sub-01_T1w.nii.gz\nGot nothing\n```\n\nConfirmed bug.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475511889,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE1MzQzNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251153434"},"message":"how old is your git -annex there?  not sure when --raw was introduced but:\n\n```\n*$\u003e /opt/git-annex/old/git-annex version --raw\n5.20151116-g76139a9\n```\n\nand then in your case I guess datalad should have reported of having no git-annex at all... what does it report for \n\n```\n$\u003e python -c 'from datalad.support.external_versions import external_versions; print repr(external_versions[\"cmd:annex\"])'\n```\n\n?\n\nand theoretically first use of AnnexRepo should have failed demanding a newer git-annex.  indeed could be related to swallowing everything in get","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475511969,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE1Mzc5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251153790"},"message":"FWIW --raw was added  in\n\n```\ncommit 7a44dacb74b6f45b7b4302ab8c744ce6075f8087\nAuthor: Joey Hess \u003cjoeyh@joeyh.name\u003e\nDate:   Thu Apr 2 15:37:39 2015 -0400\n\n    version: Add --raw\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475512020,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE1NDAzMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251154032"},"message":"So the issue is that AnnexRepo actually does check the version, but fails hard, because our code it not clever enough to ask an older git-annex for a version (for example) (external_versions.py:119). It then proceeds to treat any _not_ AnnexRepo as what it is, which in turn let's datalad fall back on plain GitRepo, which in turn causes all annex-related functionality to become unavailable.\n\nI think the core bug here is that we pretend not ot have an annex whenever we cannot work with the git-annex installation. `AnnexRepo.__init__` needs to do more careful testing and report a _dedicated_ exception that we do not auto-catch upstairs.\n\nIn general I dislike that we have a fixed minimal version, because some functionality is not available in an older version, but do not actually know whether we need this. Therefore, I support having a decorator that allows us to tag individual bits with version requirements.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475512085,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE1NDMwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251154307"},"message":"The actual swallowing happens in `Dataset.repo`, nothing is swallowed in `get` for this issue.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475512123,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE1NDQ4Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251154486"},"message":"I installed the oldest possible git-annex version that I could simply install, and would throw some kind of error.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475512626,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE1NjU4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251156587"},"message":"yeap -- also reconfirmed locally with a version before --raw was introduced.\nI thought about such a decorator myself, but decided against it.  Way too many moving targets atm with git-annex, us asking to add features etc.  Failing some pieces while keeping other pieces going with older annex sounded like just defraying the problem, actually worsening UX (IMHO it is better demand recent one once, than failing at different corners while kinda working some times), asking for trouble also -- that is why I did have that really hard exception thrown. Ok with me to get a dedicated exception, but not sure if those catches should be that wild, as you have already commented on many of them ;-) for now though may be just indeed making a helper `analyze_swallowed_exception(exc)` which would propagate SystemExit, and this annex dedicated one could well be due for a quick fix there","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475515833,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgxMDYxNjY2NQ=="},"added":["WIP"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475516127,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgxMDYyMzA4NQ=="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475516127,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50ODEwNjIzMDg2"},"added":[],"removed":["WIP"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1475516260,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE3MjEyNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251172124"},"message":"Current state in #959:\n\n```\n% datalad get sub-01/anat/sub-01_T1w.nii.gz\n2016-10-03 19:36:05,559 [ERROR  ] stderr| git-annex: unrecognized option `--raw'\n| \n| Usage: git-annex version  [option ...]\n| \n| To see additional options common to all commands, run: git annex help options (cmd.py:406)\n2016-10-03 19:36:05,560 [ERROR  ] Failed to run ['git', 'annex', 'version', '--raw'] under None. Exit code=1. out= err=git-annex: unrecognized option `--raw'\n| \n| Usage: git-annex version  [option ...]\n| \n| To see additional options common to all commands, run: git annex help options\n| \n| \n|  (cmd.py:352)\n2016-10-03 19:36:05,590 [ERROR  ] git-annex of version \u003e= 6.20160808 is missing. Install  git-annex-standalone  from NeuroDebian (http://neuro.debian.net). You have version 5.20150327+git27-g6af24b6-1~nd80+1 [annexrepo.py:_check_git_annex_version:259] (OutdatedExternalDependency) (main.py:270)\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475517545,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MTE3Nzk0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/897#issuecomment-251177948"},"message":"great.  I will check later how it would look on raiders where some anatomicals aren't avail","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1476486523,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgyNDY2MjA1Mw=="},"added":["in progress"],"removed":[]},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476616536,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50ODI1MDgxNTk3"},"status":2},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1476616540,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50ODI1MDgxNjA5"},"added":[],"removed":["in progress"]}]}